    "narrative": "Our primary engine today is **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who commands the highest score of 74.26, fueled by a soft matchup against Martinez (4.91 xERA). Despite a marginal park penalty, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains our most essential asset due to his elite floor and speed profile, which is critical given our aggressive pursuit of Stolen Bases. High-floor plays in favorable environments highlight our remaining top-tier starters: **Luis Arraez** (69.53) and **Dylan Beavers** (69.51) benefit significantly from strong SP matchups and favorable lineup positioning. **Dylan Beavers** in particular sees a massive 16% park-factor boost that elevates his ceiling, making him a prime candidate to anchor our offensive output alongside **Jung Hoo Lee**, who also exploits the favorable R-handed pitching environment.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the card was keeping **Bryce Harper** on the bench with a 55.05 rating. While **Bryce Harper** carries immense pedigree, his efficiency against Weathers (3.46 xERA) failed to surpass the platoon-advantaged profiles of **Jonathan Aranda** (64.35) and **Daulton Varsho** (60.97). We are prioritizing the cumulative efficiency of our outfield and utility spots over individual star power to maximize our 5x5 category targets. Caution is advised with **Cal Raleigh** (46.33) and **Yainer Diaz** (45.97); both face formidable arms in Eovaldi and Burke, respectively. Their scores have been squeezed by SP skill penalties, requiring us to monitor their game caps closely as we navigate the day\u2019s marginal hitting conditions.",
